            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='20'>Price vs. Rating </run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Times New Roman' fontsize='14'>This section analyzes how average price and average review ratings interact across 100 book genres. By plotting each genre as a single aggregated point, we can quickly identify categories that command higher prices, those that consistently earn stronger ratings, and those that diverge from overall market patterns. Bubble size reflects total review volume, allowing us to distinguish niche genres from those with broad consumer engagement. Together, these metrics provide a clear view of how pricing, perceived quality, and reader interest align or diverge, across the book marketplace.</run>
